### Manual requests against the running API (`dotnet run --project src/IdleHold.Api`).
### In VS Code, install the "REST Client" extension and click "Send Request" above each block.
### The session is a cookie, so run "Start a guest session" (or sign in) first; the client keeps it.

@host = http://localhost:5085

### List game content
GET {{host}}/content

### Start a guest session (an anonymous account with its own hold)
POST {{host}}/account/guest

### Who is signed in (a guest has no e-mail)
GET {{host}}/account/me

### Get my player state (caught up to now)
GET {{host}}/me/player

### Start chopping pine
POST {{host}}/me/player/action
Content-Type: application/json

{ "actionId": "cut-pine" }

### Craft the chipped stone axe (needs 3 twigs and 2 pebbles; 409 without them or once you own it)
POST {{host}}/me/player/action
Content-Type: application/json

{ "actionId": "craft-chipped-stone-axe" }

### Stop the current action
DELETE {{host}}/me/player/action

### Sign up: a guest keeps its hold
POST {{host}}/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "player@example.test", "password": "a long enough password" }

### Sign in (a guest session's hold is deleted)
POST {{host}}/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "player@example.test", "password": "a long enough password" }

### Sign out (a guest is deleted with its hold)
POST {{host}}/account/logout
